    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into favorable matchups against pitchers with high expected ERAs, led by our strongest play, **James Wood** (78.42). Facing Chandler, **James Wood** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and his elite 0.420 xwOBA, anchoring our outfield. Close behind is **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), whose massive 14% park boost and platoon advantage against Mahle make him a high-upside start. We are also capitalizing on **Brice Turang** (73.40) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.03); **Brice Turang** earns significant value from his leadoff spot and a high stolen base probability against a slow-delivery pitcher, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite facing Sproat, as his dynamic platoon edge and hitting environment continue to offer elite production potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (47.49). Despite his pedigree, **Austin Riley** was squeezed out by a combination of a tough matchup against McLean and a low batting order position that limited his overall efficiency score. He fell just short of **Kyle Karros** (57.47) and **Dalton Rushing** (47.79) due to the sheer volume of high-efficiency outfield and middle-infield options we are running today. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Corbin Carroll** closely as their lineups remain pending; if their projected spots shift significantly lower in the order, we may need to pivot. Additionally, while **Seiya Suzuki** (64.03) remains a strong play, we are keeping a close eye on the wind report, as the \"Wind In\" warning provides a slight drag on his power potential today.",
